From 60aede62fdc6078815d10ed7a8eff09ed8d2440a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhaosiying12138 <neucszhaopeng2016@163.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 03:54:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 36/42] gpu-compute,vega: serve atomics natively and stop
 aborting on a display string

Two defects, each of which killed a Qwen3.5 TP1 lane after it had already
retired hundreds of dispatches, and each repaired at the layer that owns the
behaviour rather than at the instruction that happened to expose it.

The host-native vector memory path served only ReadReq and WriteReq, so the
first global atomic aborted the run with "unsupported host-native vector
command SwapReq" -- a vLLM lane at dispatch 444 and an SGLang lane at 1413.
Implement the operation the way AbstractMemory::access already does it for
every other memory: read the current value, hand the packet its pre-operation
copy, apply the request's AtomicOpFunctor, and store the result. The packet's
buffer aliases the instruction's per-lane d_data slot, so that copy is exactly
what an atomic-with-return reads back. The whole sequence runs inside one
simulator event, so no other simulated access interleaves and the operation is
atomic in the sense the ISA requires. This is functor-generic: it covers every
GPU atomic, not the add that happened to fail. A swap arriving without a
functor still fails closed.

Separately, opSelectorToRegSym aborted the simulation on any operand selector
it had no name for. Every one of its forty-odd callers writes to a disassembly
stream; the function has no part in instruction semantics. Selector 248,
1/(2*pi), therefore killed a vLLM lane at 444 dispatches even though
operand.hh reads that constant correctly and vop_semantics.hh already knows its
f16 encoding -- only the display string was missing. Complete the table with
the eight named selectors it lacked (248-255) and downgrade the default from
fatal to a placeholder that names the unknown selector, so a cosmetic gap
becomes visible in a trace instead of ending a run. Adding only case REG_PI
would have left seven more selectors able to end a run hours in.

Evidence is a public-HIP capsule with a negative control: on the pre-fix binary
it reproduces the production panic verbatim, and on the fixed binary 256 lanes
atomically incrementing one address leave it at exactly base+256 while the
returned values form exactly the sequence base..base+255 -- 256 distinct, no
duplicates, no gaps, which a post-operation return or a lost update would fail.

